WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.170
 I love fear.

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:03.340
Fear is fuel.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:05.950
I kind of joke, but not
really, that I put fear

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:10.660
in my bowl of cereal in
the morning, and I eat it.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.340
I was not an athlete as a kid.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:15.360
I say that I was actually
allergic to exercise.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.440
So the fact that
working out is actually

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:20.410
my life's work is
astonishing, definitely to me,

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:22.960
and everyone around me.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.690
I am a reformed lawyer
turned ultramarathoner.

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:27.850
I'm Head Instructor
and Vice President

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:30.220
of Fitness Programming
at Peloton,

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.280
and I am here to start fires.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.330
We can absolutely
change our stories.

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:36.580
I am living proof.

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:42.700
If you're coming to this class
expecting me to teach you

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.770
the nuts and bolts
of fitness, that's

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:45.970
not going to happen today.

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:48.520
In my MasterClass, we're
going to be applying

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.160
the principles of
movement, and fitness

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.530
to business and storytelling.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:56.500
We're going to talk about
ways to plot dreams using

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.660
things like journaling and
visualization techniques.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:02.410
Even if you don't consider
yourself an athlete;

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:05.950
even if you also think that
you are allergic to exercise.

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:10.060
The principles of
endurance, power, strength,

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:12.730
they apply to every
industry, everyday.

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:14.890
Two weeks before I started
working at Peloton,

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:16.840
I was diagnosed as
a type 1 diabetic.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:18.700
My pancreas stopped
producing insulin.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:21.050
Completely unexpected;
and in that moment,

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:23.620
I had to decide, "do I
crumble, or do I pivot?

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:28.660
Am I a victim to this, or am
I still victorious, despite?"

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:30.340
Movement is therapy for me.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:33.490
The process of training, and
having something to focus on,

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:36.310
and having something that
was for me, changed my life.

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:38.410
Now we are going to get
you from wherever you

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:40.335
are to where you want to be.

00:01:40.335 --> 00:01:41.710
We're going to
get uncomfortable.

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:45.820
This class is for anyone who
has a glimmer of curiosity about

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:48.040
what's possible for themselves.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:51.370
I'm Robin Arzón, and
this is my MasterClass.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:01.850
This is baby's
first MasterClass!

